Hi Mike,

Thanks for your input. I’m glad you are finding Deducer useful.

Regarding your requests:

1. Yes, I’d recommend working with them in a numeric coding. Rank based tests such as the ones mentioned are meant for both ordinal and numeric outcomes. In general, ordinal analyses in R are performed on numeric variables.

2. One way that I like doing this visualization is with a bubble chart (is that the right name?).

3. When you run a plot, there is a menu in the JavaGD window allowing you to save in your preferred format (png, pdf, …)

Best,
Ian

